---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { CARE_PLAN, FREE_BUILD } from '../config';
---

<Base
  title="Free build terms"
  description="The plain-English terms of the free website build: what's free, what's not, who owns what, and how handoff works."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container container--narrow">
      <span class="eyebrow">Terms</span>
      <h1>The free build, in writing.</h1>
      <p class="lede" style="margin-top: var(--space-4);">
        This is the plain-English version of what we agree to before a build
        starts. You'll get it as a one-page document to sign — same content,
        no extra fine print.
      </p>

      <div class="stack" style="margin-top: var(--space-6);">
        <h2>What's free</h2>
        <p>
          One website of up to {FREE_BUILD.maxPages} pages, built from your
          intake answers, with {FREE_BUILD.revisionRounds} revision round
          included. First working draft within {FREE_BUILD.draftTimeline} of
          intake.
        </p>

        <h2>What's not free</h2>
        <p>
          Web apps and custom functionality, ongoing edits and content,
          photography and logo design, pages beyond
          {FREE_BUILD.maxPages}, and ongoing growth services — all quoted
          plainly in writing if you want them, never assumed.
        </p>

        <h2>Ownership</h2>
        <p>
          You own the site. Your domain is registered in your own account
          from day one. At launch we transfer the code and hosting into
          accounts in your name, or host it for you on the
          {CARE_PLAN.name} — your choice, changeable later.
        </p>

        <h2>Hosting</h2>
        <p>
          The build is free. Running any website costs hosting: roughly
          $0–20 a month if you run it yourself, or {CARE_PLAN.price} if we
          handle hosting, updates, and support. If you ever leave the
          {CARE_PLAN.name}, we hand everything over within 5 business days
          at no charge.
        </p>

        <h2>Images and content</h2>
        <p>
          You confirm you have the right to use the photos, logos, and
          testimonials you give us. We only publish testimonials you have
          written permission to use.
        </p>

        <h2>Our archive copy</h2>
        <p>
          We keep an archived copy of the finished site and may show the
          work as part of our portfolio. If you'd rather we didn't, say so
          and we won't.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
